## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical batch ingestion, per-record contracts, privacy masking, and idempotent upserts in a common lakehouse pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Data contracts, masking, bad_data routing
- Iceberg schema evolution, upserts, unique keys
- Test plans for duplicates, new fields, and schema drift

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(record) {
  const required = ["user_id","event_ts","event_type"];
  for (const k of required) if (!(k in record)) return false;
  // simple mask
  if (record.payload) record.payload.pii = null;
  return true;
}
```

```javascript
// MERGE-like upsert (pseudocode)
MERGE INTO iceberg.fact AS t
USING staging AS s
ON t.user_id = s.user_id AND t.event_ts = s.event_ts
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests privacy-first, scalable analytics across regions with data contracts.

## Key Concepts

- Per-region pseudonymization
- Iceberg upserts
- Event-time windows and lateness handling
- Immutable audits and data contracts
- Spark vs Flink trade-offs for streaming

## Code Example

```javascript
// Region-aware salt hash (Node.js)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function saltedHash(region, id, salts){
  const salt = salts[region] ?? salts.default;
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(id + salt).digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency and audit coverage?
